  "paper_id": "ccs-2025-breaking-and-provably-restoring-authentication-a-formal-c23ca57a",
  "title": "Breaking and Provably Restoring Authentication: A Formal Analysis of SPDM 1.2 including Cross-Protocol Attacks",
  "abstract": "The SPDM (Security Protocol and Data Model) protocol is a standard under development by the DMTF consortium, and supported by major industry players including Broadcom, Cisco, Dell, Google, HP, IBM, Intel, and NVIDIA. SPDM 1.2 is a complex protocol that aims to provide platform security, for example for communicating hardware components or cloud computing scenarios. SPDM is the core security mechanism of PCI Express (PCIe) and Compute Express Link (CXL).",
